The review document has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/python-gaps/pygap-03-python-utils-parse-datetime.md`.

**Key findings at a glance:**

- **3 Medium**: RFC3339 offset not normalized (inconsistent with naive branches), sub-second precision lost for non-RFC3339 inputs, `extract_datetime` breaks on Python naive datetimes with microseconds
- **3 Low**: Leap seconds rejected with generic error, date-only path untested, duplicated offset construction

The core RFC3339 offset math, UTC assumption for naive inputs, date-only midnight handling, DST safety, malformed input rejection, and year bounds are all verified correct. The main gaps are the sub-second precision handling and the offset normalization inconsistency.
